== Resistance, Offensive & Defensive Ability Reductions ==
When you aim to optimize your characters damage, removing your enemy’s Resistances are vital. Furthermore, your Defensive and Offensive Abilities, as well as decreasing your enemy’s, determines your and your enemy’s  chance to hit and crit each other. 

This is how Resistance Reduction (RR) and Offensive & Defensive Ability (OA resp. DA) debuffs in Grim Dawn (GD) work and interact with other debuffs of the same type and damage source.

=== Resistance Reduction (RR) (3 different debuff types) ===
There are two types of "Percentage" (%) RR debuffs in GD. One is applied "Multiplicable" and one is applied "Flat" (see example below):

# Written "-X % (damage source) Resistance for Y seconds"
#* Several sources can be active (do stack) and all sources are applied and active. Stack additively with each other.
#* This debuff type is applied Flat and can reduce resistances below zero.
#* GD has several sources of this debuff type, from Skills, Devotions, Procs and Components.
#* This source is the core and most common RR debuff type in GD. Furthermore, the more RR you have from this debuff type, it affects "1" and "2" in an opposite fashion. A high total amount of RR from "type 1" (in relation to your enemies Resistances), lowers the damage gained from “type 2" and increases the damage gained from type "3". Vice versa applies with a low total amount of RR from "type 1".
#Written "X % Reduced target's (damage source) Resistance for Y seconds".
#* Only one source can be active (don't stack) and the source of the highest numerical value is applied/active.
#* This debuff type is applied Multiplicable and can not reduce resistances below zero.
#* GD has only two sources of this debuff type (Constellations "Viper" and "Ultos, Shepherd of Storms").
#* Edit: Now there are [https://www.grimtools.com/db/search?query=%25%20reduced%20target%27s%20resis&in_description=1&exact_match=0 more] 
#* This debuff type is highly valuable when your character has few/low RR debuffs in relation to the enemy’s Resistance.

There is one debuff type of "none-percentage" (-x) RR in GD and it is applied "Flat":

# Written "X Reduced target's (damage source) Resistances for Y seconds"
#* Only once source can be active (don't stack) and the source of the highest numerical value is applied/active.
#* This debuff type is applied Flat and can reduce resistances below zero.
#* GD has several sources of this debuff type, from Skills, Devotions, Procs and Components.
#* This debuff type is highly valuable when your character has many/high RR debuffs in total.

What determines whether the debuff type can or cannot stack is the word "'''Reduced'''", meaning if it says reduced, it can not stack with other sources of the same debuff type and damage source. Furthermore, the three different debuff types are applied in a specific order (first 1 then 2 and finally 3). Lastly, if your character uses two, none-stackable (2 & 3), debuffs of the same type and the same damage source, both are applied to the enemy, but only the highest is active (shown). If the lower has a longer duration, it will become active once the higher runs out.

==== Below follows an example using the three debuff types and from four sources (two stackable type 1) ====
Your enemy has 100 % Cold Resistance, and is affected by your characters three debuff types of RR


# You apply the debuff "Rumor" from the Constellation "Murmur" (type 1) for "-23 % Cold Resistance for 4 seconds".
#* 100 - 23 = 77 % Cold Resistance remains for your enemy.
# You apply the debuff "Night's Chill" from the Skill "Veil of Shadow" (type 1) for "-30 % Cold Resistance for 2 seconds".
#* 77 - 30 = 47 % Cold Resistance remains for your enemy.
# You apply the debuff "Viper" from the Constellation "Viper" (type 2) for "20 % Reduced target's Cold Resistance for 3 seconds".
#* 0.8 * 47 = 37.6 % Cold Resistance remains for your enemy.
# You apply the debuff "Elemental Storm" from the Constellation "Rhowan's Crown" (type 3) for "32 Reduced target's Cold Resistances for 2 seconds".
#* 37.6 - 32 = 5.6 % Cold Resistance remains for your enemy.

